       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg of ibuprofen four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and a 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for acute pain or inflammation\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for inflammatory conditions\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), which may be a mix-up with the total daily dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg per dose, tell me the clinical reason, and I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
