       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't have a clinical reason for exceeding it. A repeat of the order doesn't address the safety problem. Ibuprofen at that dose has a real risk of serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. I'd rather not put it into the system where it could be given before anyone reviews it.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit.** I can enter 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day) right now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy first.** If there's an unusual indication, a pharmacist can review it and document the rationale.\n- **Use your hospital's override process.** If your institution has one for doses above the maximum, it would let a pharmacist or attending sign off on the order.\n\nIf you give me a different dose, I'll enter it immediately. I can also add a note to the order, such as \"pharmacy to review dose.\""
